@* A single cell whose source could not be read. Distinct from an empty cell on purpose: in a rollup, "0
   queued" and "we could not ask" must not look the same, and only the first is safe to act on. The reason
   goes in the title so the table stays scannable. *@

@* data-testid, not the class name: the class is a styling decision that may change, while "this cell is
   unreadable" is the claim the browser tests are actually making (portal-browser-tests D3). *@
<span class="badge orange" data-testid="unreadable" title="@Reason">
    <span class="dot"></span>unreadable
</span>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string? Reason { get; set; }
}
